codex
The report recommends keeping the budgeted comparison and adding the certified offline reference, while withholding attribution that depends on unfinished searches. It also corrects the main numerical overstatements: all 90 screened outputs were BASE, the uncapped file contains 17 completed cases, and 8.9 seconds is their overall median—not the easy-group median. I’m checking the report’s citations and calculations before printing it.
